Fixed. The bug was in `src/import_merge.ts:7` — the duplicate check compared URLs with raw string equality (`b.url === inc.url`), which is case-sensitive. Since a URL's hostname is case-insensitive, `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` didn't match `https://example.com/a`.

The fix normalizes both URLs through `new URL(u).href` (which lowercases the hostname) before comparing. Invalid strings fall back to the raw value.

Verified:
- Case-only hostname difference → merged into 1 entry, tags unioned (`["x","y"]`), existing entry preserved.
- Different path → appended as a second entry.
- No existing match → appended unchanged.


